From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:21:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 146/342] meson_saradc: the S905's SAR ADC, the ODROID-C2's
 analog inputs

/dev/misc/adc/0 (header pin 40) and /dev/misc/adc/1 (pin 37) read as
millivolts, 0 to 1.8 V; an ioctl gives the converter's value too, and its
internal references for a self-test. A sample is the mean of 8
conversions, polled, with the lock the converter's other user, the system
control firmware, keeps in its DELAY register. The firmware's setup stays
when it made one; the switches that can drive an input are never set.
Readings are corrected piecewise by the five internal references (ground
to 1.8 V in quarters): on the ODROID-C2 they read 0, 249, 506, 765 and
1020, exact after the correction. Facts: the port's
docs/m27-geekport-facts.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
